Insert a coarse-pointer block just before the reduced-motion block.
old: `@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){`
new:
`@media (pointer:coarse){
  .iconbtn{width:44px;height:44px}
  .iconbtn.small{width:40px;height:40px}
  .iconbtn.spdbtn,.iconbtn.spdbtn.small{width:auto}
  .spdbtn{min-width:44px}
  .spdbtn.small{min-width:40px}
  .ttswrap{gap:8px}
  .expal{padding:8px 4px}
  .chip{padding:12px 16px}
  .btn.small{padding:12px 16px}
  .mode.small2{padding:11px 14px}
  .voicetoast .close{padding:10px 12px;font-size:22px}
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){`
The order matters: `.iconbtn.spdbtn` must come after `.iconbtn.small`, otherwise the speed button gets a fixed width.

old:
`  if(navigator.clipboard && navigator.clipboard.writeText){
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(txt).then(done).catch(() => {});
  }`
new:
`  const legacy = () => {
    try{
      const ta = document.createElement('textarea');
      ta.value = txt; ta.setAttribute('readonly','');
      ta.style.cssText = 'position:fixed;top:0;left:0;opacity:0;font-size:16px';
      document.body.appendChild(ta);
      ta.focus(); ta.select(); ta.setSelectionRange(0, txt.length);
      const ok = document.execCommand('copy');
      document.body.removeChild(ta);
      if(ok) done();
    }catch(e){}
  };
  if(navigator.clipboard && navigator.clipboard.writeText){
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(txt).then(done).catch(legacy);
  } else {
    legacy();
  }`
